&lt;p class=&quot;has-paragraph-md-font-size wp-block-paragraph&quot;&gt;AIA Maine COTE Award for Historic Adaptive Reuse of a Commercial Institution&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;wp-block-media-text__content&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;wp-block-heading  has-heading-4-font-size&quot;&gt;Designing for superior energy efficiency&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wp-block-paragraph&quot;&gt;Harriman used its skills in sustainable design to transform the empty historic building into a net-positive charter school building. This was accomplished by redesigning the building&rsquo;s thermal envelope, roof and attic design, and improving natural ventilation. We also added LED lighting and controls, thermal efficient windows and glazing, and a modern HVAC system.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wp-block-paragraph&quot;&gt;296 photovoltaic panels were installed on the roof to provide a sustainable energy harvesting source. The school uses approximately 77,000 kWh annually, leaving a &ldquo;net positive&rdquo; of 13,000 kWh of clean, renewable power. This power offsets energy needs of adjacent greenhouses and other facilities on campus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

