&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #e03e2d;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please add all the pertinent project information:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client:&lt;/strong&gt; Hunter&apos;s Shop &apos;n Save&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Type:&lt;/strong&gt; New Construction&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Size:&lt;/strong&gt; 16,000 SF&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Contact:&lt;/strong&gt; Mark Lee and Zach Smith&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recognition:&lt;/strong&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Hunter&rsquo;s Shop &lsquo;n Save is the first store in the country to utilize FlexCube, an innovative refrigeration system which relies on a more environmentally friendly coolant, A2L, to chill perishables.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;wp-block-list &quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The store incorporates five FlexCube units. Each can chill 84 linear feet of multi-deck produce cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The units are mounted on top of produce cases and the meat and dairy coolers to avoid wasting precious floor space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eight highly efficient heat pumps handle the store&rsquo;s HVAC. Waste heat from maintains the store at a comfortable 68-degrees year-round.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excess heat is transferred to the adjacent Walgreens drugstore for free.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hunter&rsquo;s Shop &lsquo;n Save owners credit the integrated mechanical system with reducing their electric bills by 66%.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

